{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/334370-from-cmage-to-nhunter","id":334370,"title":"From cMage to nHunter!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T11:21:35-08:00","id":334370,"title":"From cMage to nHunter!","content":"So, it is some old idea I've thought about.<br /> <br /> I like organizations- the more the merrier if you ask me. This is why I really like Vigil and Ascension- both of them have powerful organizations who work for occult agendas. In the end, I like Hunter better, so I've thought why not to create compacts/ conspiracies inspired by the traditions/crafts/conventions/etc?<br /> <br /> so here are the two ideas I've thought about long time ago- maybe I'll think on some others later. Fell more than welcomed to add your own!<br /> <br /> The Theater of Tragedies (Wu Keng)- demon hunters, both lesser and greater- although they don't actually &quot;hunt&quot; demons. They trick them. The are a modern creation based on an older version of the group, which have used the traditional cross dressing tradition in order to trick demons and null their pacts. Each member of the organization has an &quot;alternative Cover&quot; which is activate once they are dressed as the opposite gender, and any kind of supernatural effect which targets a specific individual (especially demonic pacts) target the alternative identity and their true identity as two different individuals. That way, they can make a pact with a demons, but when the demons wish to get his side in the deal they simply destroy the &quot;Cover&quot;. While it also destroys what they gained from the pact, they can &quot;cash&quot; the effect in order to get Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> The Ashen Collective (Solifacti)- not as nice as their previous incarnation. They hail from the Dark Ages, as a secret order of alchemists who search after the concept of &quot;soul&quot;. They believe that souls are the key for the creation of the Philosopher's Stone, and that by creating it they could achieve immortality. They also believe that the soul is found in one of the organs of the human body, so they sometimes do some.. unethical.. things in order to advance their knowledge in how the soul is composed. They are extremely interested in the Divine Fire and prometheans, especially when they compare their anatomy to one of a &quot;real human&quot;, yet they usually hunt for Pandorans and Flux (hence the &quot;Ashen&quot; in their name). They prefer to deal with the Fire when it is more &quot;static&quot; and &quot;stable&quot;, and so it is a lot more controllable. They use the captured Flux in order to create &quot;reactive automatons&quot;- that is, machines and creatures which awaken to life only when exposed to the Divine Fire- or one of their elixirs, which are made from stolen organs.<br /> <br /> your ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T11:39:40-08:00","id":334393,"title":"","content":"Have you seen my Knights Errant? I came with the idea of Convention to create Compact like groups that aren't actually groups. I think that would suite the Wu Keng quite well, rather than an organisation of demon hunting cross-dressers you have a wide verity of families, master/apprentice, and solo practitioners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T18:05:55-08:00","id":334712,"title":"","content":"I would expand the Wu Keng in scope and abilities. How would having a cover protect a Wu Keng from losing humanity by making a deal with an infernal demon? Do they gain protection from changeling pacts too through cover? And converting pacts into dread powers seems weird when only infernal demons can actually grant supernatural powers, since the unbound can provide supernatural merits at best. <br /> <br /> I'd give them an endowment based on their covers, &quot;masks&quot; seems like a good name for them, I'd let them have several &quot;covers&quot; and I'd extend their cosmic identity fraud to include something like demonic legend: the Wu Keng might be a powerful business man, a medium, a deadly martial artist, etc, depending on the mask, losing morality/integrity reduces the mask when dealing with infernal deals.<br /> <br /> Just how I would do it anyway. <br /> <br /> As for the Ashen Collective, are you aware that there is a cult formed by the Mekhet that can surgically remove the soul, transplanting the soul from one person to the other, or eating them? I'd have the Ashen Collective have found the soul organ, making them body thieves who harvest the souls of the recently dead, and perform grisly experiments with them. What happens if you transplant a human soul into an animal? A dead body? What happens if you transplant a human soul into a supernatural, or transplant a supernatural soul into a human? <br /> <br /> They could even still be promethean oriented, as soulless bodies, I'm sure the Ashen Collective might love transplanting human souls into prometheans and watching the results. And imagine the delicious irony of promethean bad guys who want to give prometheans souls, only for it to be a very bad thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:32:05-08:00","id":336304,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Champions of Industry (Technocracy):</b> </span> <div align=\"center\">&quot;Blood, sweat, and tears are mankind's magic.&quot;</div> <br /> More of a Convention than a Conspiracy, the name &quot;Champions of Industry&quot; covers a wide variety of labor unions and inventor's clubs that have become &quot;clued in&quot; to the Vigil. Groups have cropped up since the Industrial Revolution all through-out the industrialized world. Their Endowment goes by many different names, but the most general term is &quot;Fruits of Labor&quot;; beneficiaries begin developing a sort of rudimentary machine empathy or gain the ability to work for hours without fatigue.<br /> <br /> They go after the Supernatural because they're <i>relics</i>; they have no place in this modern world, and should make way for human progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:53:01-08:00","id":337383,"title":"","content":"I have to be honest about something. I genuinely feel that in some cases &quot;hunting monsters&quot; can get shoehorned into groups where it doesn't belong. If you look at some of the groups I've worked on - Hakollel and the Wylde Society for example; yeah they might hunt monsters but it's not the core of the group.<br /> <br /> Les Mysteriis is the cannon group I feel that's worst affected. I think that their desire to exterminate Werewolves is much less interesting than the natural conflict that would arise from their completely incompatible world views.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I digress. I think that Champions of Industry is a pretty cool concept, but I don't think they should be monster hunters. Instead I think they should focus on industry and occasionally defend themselves from anti-change monsters. A vampire who doesn't get this new fangled &quot;car&quot; and wants to keep that delightful smell of horses in the street for example.<br /> <br /> Though it is cool to see someone else use Convention <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:07:00-08:00","id":337686,"title":"","content":"Raven, that's not so much a personal opinion but a flat out fact of the hunter line. <br /> <br /> The talbot group is a support group for crying out loud, and there are several compacts where hunter really isn't the first term to describe them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:47:04-08:00","id":337740,"title":"","content":"Hunt is a very flexible word that has less pre-loaded context than some believe.<br /> <br /> Also, this isn't quite &quot;The Hunter must Hunt.&quot; The word used to describe all hunter's 'quest' is Vigil, which is also a word that has a very flexible meaning. The 'Hunter' Must Perform a 'Vigil'.<br /> <br /> Some people hunt monsters to be vigilant over them in the same way Liam Neeson hunts for his daughter to be vigilant over her in Taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T00:40:16-08:00","id":337861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/334370-from-cmage-to-nhunter?p=337686#post337686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Raven, that's not so much a personal opinion but a flat out fact of the hunter line.</div> </div> </div> </div> The personal opinion is that &quot;some groups have killing monsters shoehorned into their goals&quot; not &quot;I think there should be non-violent hunters&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:04:59-08:00","id":338621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/334370-from-cmage-to-nhunter?p=337861#post337861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The personal opinion is that &quot;some groups have killing monsters shoehorned into their goals&quot; not &quot;I think there should be non-violent hunters&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that was exactly what I was talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Talbot group- support group<br /> <br /> Ashwood abbey- have fun with the supernatural<br /> <br /> illuminated brotherhood- use psychotropic drugs to understand the supernatural<br /> <br /> utopia now- use supernaturals to build a utopia<br /> <br /> network zero- expose the supernatural<br /> <br /> null mysteriis- understand the supernatural<br /> <br /> Keepers of the source- ecoterrorists<br /> <br /> Actually killing supernaturals isn't in the official mission statement of any of those groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 12-12-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T01:30:51-08:00","id":338849,"title":"","content":"I don't see how that's a reply to my post. I said some groups; the groups I'm talking about are mostly not on your list.<br /> <br /> I say mostly because I do think the killing witches was shoehorned into the Keeper's goals. The Keepers have two goals - protect mother nature, prevent witches from drawing Source. Those two goals are completely unrelated <u><u>except</u></u> for the fact that the Keepers have a big misunderstanding. Personally I don't like that, and would much rather that the Keepers conflicts with witches fit better into the environmentalist mission.<br /> <br /> So basically. I don't how what you're saying ties into what I'm saying? I'm not talking about Null Mysteriis or Net0, I think both groups are fine. I'm talking about the Keepers of the Source, Les Mysterys, or in this particular thread I was mostly talking about the Champions of Industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}